That is also why Eduardo C. Corral’s moss simile is so important in the late lecture. The transcript is unstable just before the example, but the technical claim is secure. The comparison works not image-to-image, but behavior-to-behavior: $\begin{aligned}
\text{applause} \not\sim \text{moss by image}, \qquad \text{applause} \sim \text{moss by behavior},\\
\text{behavioral correspondence} \Longrightarrow \text{apparent acceleration of moss growth}.\end{aligned}$

